 "title": "JUB1 and PAPS Pathway Interactions in Kluyveromyces lactis and U.S. Department of Energy Research",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the interactions between JUB1 and the PAPS pathway in the organism Kluyveromyces lactis. JUB1-X, a synthetic transcription factor, is derived from JUB1 and expresses ATPS and PPK2, which are part of the PAPS pathway. The PAPS pathway integrates with Kluyveromyces lactis and expresses PPK2CpaN. JUB1 has various inputs, including IPTG, LacI, and galactose, and targets CYC1. The U.S. Department of Energy and the DOE Joint BioEnergy Institute are also mentioned, indicating a research context for these interactions.",
